# Line-ending policy (AHQ-211): all text files are LF — in the repo AND in
# every working tree. eol=lf (not just text=auto) so checkouts stay LF even
# under core.autocrlf=true on Windows: prettier enforces endOfLine "lf", and
# a CRLF .sh fails with "bad interpreter" under Git Bash and WSL. Binary
# files are auto-detected and left untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Exec-bit-carrying scripts, pinned explicitly: a CRLF checkout of these is
# not formatting drift but an execution failure ("bad interpreter" — the
# kernel reads the shebang line up to \r). Redundant with the * rule today;
# kept so loosening that rule can never silently break these.
*.sh text eol=lf
bin/agentic-hq.cjs text eol=lf
src/scripts/git-scripts/branching/03-squash-merge-branch/perform-squash-merge-on-branch.ts text eol=lf
